## Contained: a wrong artifact (not the subject)
A Claude session left a branch `claude/overnight-2026-11-26` whose `chem/pairenergy` models the
electric energy as `Sum_v bal-sq(|n_v|)`, lets the vertices between a +-1 pair relax to neutral, and
"checks" that a separated pair costs 2 at any distance. It drops the Faraday flux string that Gauss's
law (`chem/cover`) forces onto the connecting path; `chem/fluxsplit` already proves the least energy
grows as `min(d, N-d)` — confinement. The lemmas are valid arithmetic over a wrong model. Discard the
branch. The correct results are on `main`: `fluxsplit`, `cover`, `sectors`, `netatom`, `ringatom`,
`linkhop`, `h2plus-net`, `h2-net`, and the inertia engine `inertia`/`inertiathm`/`sylvester`.
